      "writtenOn": "2023-05-12T20:09:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need to free the previous entries (if any) and destroy the hashtable as well. You\u0027ll also have to do that at the end of the function before returning, so it might be useful to write this as:\n\n```\nif (!e) {\n        ret \u003d -ENOMEM;\n        goto free_rht;\n}\n\n...\n\nfree_rht:\n       rhashtable_free_and_destroy(...);\n       return ret; \n```\n\nAnd keep in mind that this changes the behavior of `count_plts()`; IOW it can now return a negative value.",
      "revId": "4d39554b7882b142cdfd2acb1ba255f0504938b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
